  "preamble": "Lateralization of the alveolar tap [ɾ] to [l]. In Caribbean Spanish (Puerto Rico, eastern and central Cuba, eastern Dominican Republic and Santo Domingo), the syllable-final tap often surfaces as [l]. In Polynesian, Proto-Polynesian *r (a tap) merged with *l in Samoic-Outlier languages and in Hawaiian, while Tahitian and Māori keep r.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Lateralization, Liquid Merger",
